  "heat": 3,
  "text": "Tamar outmaneuvered a patriarch and got it in writing. Genesis thirty eight, and it is a rough chapter. Tamar is married to Judah's eldest son, who dies. By custom she is given to the next brother, who also dies. Judah tells her to go live as a widow in her father's house until his third son grows up, and then he never sends for him. So she is left in limbo, no husband, no children, no standing, and no way to challenge it. Then she hears Judah is going up to Timnath to shear sheep. She takes off her widow's clothes, covers herself with a veil, and sits by the road. He does not recognise her. He propositions her, and promises a kid from the flock. And this is where she gets sharp. She asks for a pledge first. His signet, his bracelets, and his staff. His identification, essentially. Three months later, she is pregnant, and Judah is told, and he says bring her out and let her be burnt. And she sends him his own signet and staff and says, discern whose these are. And Judah says, she hath been more righteous than I.",
